Expected elements: MISSING — a timeline or scrubber expressing position within the trace

That absence is finding #1, it is P1, and my rating is 4. Nothing between the fourth button pair and the phase rail carries a track, ticks or a playhead, and no pane holds a time surface; the `1…8` strip in the Code pane scrubs one loop, not the trace. The bar has roughly 285px of empty space to its right, so the omission is not a width forcing at 1440.

Structurally the page is sound: one row of two columns, Code beside a tabbed Call Trace / Event Log region with Values below it and the Transaction pane at the right, consistent 8px gutters, consistent pane-header insets, no page scrollbar, no full-width pane.

The layout problem is that space is pooled where nothing needs it. The banner takes 185px of a 900px viewport for a 600px-wide paragraph; the tabbed region holds 115px of dead height under its last frame; the identity bar holds a 285px void. Meanwhile the Values and Transaction panes are sliced mid-row at the viewport edge, and the Code pane clips its own source at its right border.

Highest-priority fixes: (1) restore the timeline into the bar's existing slack; (2) move the tabbed region's 115px of empty height into the Values pane below it, which is the pane currently being cut.

Rating: 4/10

